{
  "$doc": "Registry of the ChatGPT chats used for image generation, grouped by PURPOSE. Every image-gen script (repurpose/gen-batch*.js, generate-broll-wlw.js, generate-image.js, etc.) consults this via repurpose/chat-pool.js. A ChatGPT chat degrades past ~25 images (stops rendering OR returns off-prompt/style-contaminated images), so each chat is capped and auto-rotated. Chats are also keyed by purpose so different visual styles (cinematic b-roll vs text-slide carousels vs tweet renders) never share a chat and cross-contaminate. Flow: getActiveUrl(purpose) -> if a chat for that purpose has count<cap, reuse it; else the caller opens a fresh chatgpt.com/ chat, generates, captures the /c/<id> URL, and registerNewChat() REPLACES the full one (replace-then-delete: retired chats are dropped, so at steady state there is ~1 active object per purpose). recordImage(purpose) increments only on a SUCCESSFUL save. markDead(purpose) drops a chat that was manually deleted in the UI (conversation-not-found) so a fresh one is made. Seeded empty on 2026-06-07 because the prior hand-recorded persistent chats were all overloaded/contaminated; the pool creates fresh chats on first use per purpose.",
